      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for:\n\n- \"Cost, Insurance, and Freight\" (FOB does not apply until 2020 changes). \n- Costs:  pays for freight and customs duties.\n- Insurance: The seller is required to have insurance that covers all risks of loss or damage up to the time they deliver the goods to the carrier or a designated third-party at the named point of departure, which is known as FAS.\n- The risk then passes from the seller to the buyer once the goods have been handed to the carrier or the designated third-party at the FAS point, at which point the buyer is responsible for any further transportation, customs clearance, or loss or damage.",
